    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="structllvm_1_1_offset_span" kindref="compound">OffsetSpan</ref> - Used internally by <computeroutput><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_object_size_offset_visitor" kindref="compound">ObjectSizeOffsetVisitor</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Represents a point in memory as a pair of allocated bytes before and after it.</para>
<para><computeroutput>Before</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>After</computeroutput> fields are signed values. It makes it possible to represent out-of-bound access, e.g. as a result of a GEP, at the expense of not being able to represent very large allocation. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
